# Local-only by policy, not by size: the evidence tree is the audit archive whose
# purpose is that a claim can be taken to AWS Support by request id and FULL ARN
# (see check_redaction.py's docstring). It is never distributed; the release path
# is results/ plus the Markdown deliverables, which the redaction gate scans.
evidence/

# The EC2 runner's local bookkeeping: the instance, subnet, security-group and VPC ids it
# provisioned, the code tarball it uploads, and output pulled back from S3 for review. Three of
# those id shapes are redaction targets (check_redaction.py's `vpc-or-subnet-id` pattern), and a
# file that needs a waiver on every run is a file that trains a reader to waive things. The
# runner's SOURCE is tracked; only its resolved ids are not.
runner/.state/

# Environments and caches
.venv/
.venv-*/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
f1_config/.wheel_cache/
.DS_Store
